## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates practical knowledge of serverless data pipelines on GCP, including error handling, data enrichment, and idempotent design patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Storage triggers and CSV validation
- Header normalization and PII masking
- Pub/Sub as a decoupling layer between ingestion and processing
- Dataflow streaming for real-time enrichment and aggregation
- BigQuery insertId for deduplication and idempotency
- Least-privilege IAM bindings
- Exponential backoff retry strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function: triggered on GCS object finalization
exports.processTelemetry = (event, context) => {
  const file = event.bucket + '/' + event.name;

  return validateAndPublish(file)
    .then(() => console.log(`Processed: ${file}`))
    .catch(err => {
      console.error(`Error processing ${file}:`, err);
      throw err; // Triggers retry with exponential backoff
    });
};

async function validateAndPublish(file) {
  const [content] = await bucket.file(event.name).download();
  const rows = parseCSV(content);
  const validRows = rows.filter(validateRowSchema);
  const normalizedRows = validRows.map(normalizeHeaders).map(maskPII);

  await publisher.publish(normalizedRows);
}
```

## Evaluation Criteria
- Correct trigger configuration and bucket path pattern
- Schema validation logic implementation
- PII masking approach (field-level redaction)
- Idempotent BigQuery writes via insertId
- Appropriate retry/backoff configuration

